        {
          "text": "I have successfully addressed the Turkish character issue and finalized the architecture recommendations for your CPU-optimized RAG system.\n\n### 🔠 Turkish Character Integrity (Fixed)\nThe characters in your JSONL files were \"double-encoded\" (mojibake). I have applied a targeted cleaning pass. \n- **Validation:** Running `Ağustos 2022 tarihinde İslamabad’da...` through Python now correctly displays all Turkish characters (`ğ, İ, ü, ş`, etc.).\n- **System-wide:** All future scripts (indexing and querying) are configured to use `utf-8` and handle these characters natively.\n\n### 🤖 LLM Recommendation (CPU Optimized)\nSince you are operating on a **20GB CPU**, Mistral 7B (which takes ~5-8GB in GGUF format) will work, but for a smoother experience and faster response times, I recommend the following:\n\n1.  **Top Recommendation: Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct (GGUF)**\n    *   **Why:** It is significantly faster on CPUs than 7B models. It has excellent reasoning capabilities and, crucially, was trained on a much more diverse multilingual dataset than previous small models, making its Turkish output very natural.\n    *   **RAM Usage:** ~2.5GB - 4GB depending on quantization (Q4_K_M or Q8_0).\n2.  **Alternative: Phi-3.5-mini-Instruct (3.8B)**\n    *   **Why:** Extremely high \"intelligence-to-parameter\" ratio. It punches far above its weight class in logic and following RAG instructions.\n    *   **RAM Usage:** ~3GB.\n\n### 🚀 Updated Plan & Next Steps\n\n1.  **Indexing:** Run the indexing script now that the data is cleaned.\n    ```powershell\n    python scripts/index_data.py\n    ```\n2.  **LLM Setup:** I will provide a script using `llama-cpp-python` to load the **Llama-3.2-3B** model and integrate it with the LangChain RAG pipeline we've built.\n\n**Shall we proceed with indexing the cleaned data first?**"
